            <div class="section-header">
                <div class="section-title">About me</div>
                <h2 class="section-heading">From Molecular Biology to Machine Learning</h2>
            </div>

            <p>I am a data scientist with a PhD in plant molecular biology and
            eight years applying machine learning in industry — classical NLP,
            deep learning for vision and time series, and more recently LLM
            agents and retrieval systems in production.</p>

            <p>My doctoral work integrated transcriptomic, proteomic, genomic
            and physiological data to study plant proximity responses. The move
            into data science was less of a jump than it sounds: the constant
            has been working with messy scientific data and asking whether a
            result actually holds.</p>

            <p>Since 2018 I have led projects end to end — scoping, hiring,
            modelling, deployment — across scientific e-commerce, vertical
            farming and agritech. In 2023 I built an agent system that generated
            graph queries for researchers without a technical background, at a
            point when the tooling and patterns for doing this were still
            emerging.</p>

            <p>I am currently working on two things: independent research on
            LLM agent reliability and evaluation, and an applied project on
            molecular detection in the food chain.</p>

            <p>What interests me most is that generating results has become
            inexpensive while validating them has not. That gap is where I
            want to work.</p>

